"""Opening-bracket detector for layers.0.mlp.down_proj:3304.

This component is a "something opens here" neuron. It goes strongly negative on a
token that opens a bracketed or quoted span, and is near zero everywhere else.
Strength follows how heavy the bracket is in ordinary text:

  - round brackets "(" (and fullwidth "（") are strongest, about -2 to -3;
  - square brackets "[" and "【" are about -1;
  - curly braces "{" and "「" "『" are about -0.7;
  - opening quote-like marks (“ ‘ " |, 《, –) are weak, about -0.2 to -0.5.

Only the bare opener counts: "()", "{}", "[]", "('", "(\\" and the like are near zero,
and so are closing brackets. A leading space ("  (" vs "(") makes the opener stronger.

Predicted value is the table entry for the current token (no context is needed).
