"""Approximate a response to short pieces continuing an alphabetic word.

Vowel-led pieces are positive, especially initial y and i plus a vowel.
Longer preceding pieces strengthen the response; an unspaced preceding
piece also boosts it. A final vowel or h changes the gain, particularly
for y and i. Common grammatical endings are weaker. The small additional
rules recognize -ry, causative verb endings, and the noun ending -ency.
Vowel runs measure spelling, not pronunciation.
